  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Planning the Architecture**\n\nOkay, I\'ve got a firm grasp of the skill documentation. Now, my focus is shifting to architecting the \'Persona Writer Studio\'. I\'ve decided to build a full-stack application. It\'ll be an Express server alongside a React Vite SPA. The Express backend will be handled in `server.ts`.\n\n\n**Defining API Endpoints**\n\nI\'m now nailing down the REST API endpoints. I plan to use the Gemini API (`gemini-3.5-flash`) for manuscript generation and evaluation. The API will offer endpoints for generating manuscripts (`/api/generate-manuscript`), evaluating them (`/api/evaluate-manuscript`), retrieving manuscript archives (`/api/manuscripts`), and saving new manuscripts or sessions (`/api/manuscripts`). I envision a React frontend (Vite SPA) to handle user interactions via three key views.\n\n\n**Visualizing Frontend Components**\n\nI\'m now visualizing the frontend components. I\'ve broken it down into three key views: a Landing View with an introductory tagline and visual representations of the editor and persona cards; an Editor View with a prompt input, AI manuscript generation or manual typing, and evaluation metrics, including a \'rewrite\' and \'save draft\' option; and finally, an Evaluation Dashboard View to facilitate comparison analysis of results from multiple persona models, highlighting detailed metrics and risk assessments.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 4
      nanos: 305653308
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
